From 60834c5fda6be5b6f2a2a0446b952be2d2b22fff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xander Burchartz <210020462+xanderburchartz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/32] iOS: platform layer, build guards and OpenGL ES 2
 through Qt

Make OpenCPN build and run on iOS (wxWidgets on Qt, static build, app
sandbox). These two parts only build together, so they are one commit.

OpenGL ES 2 through Qt:
- On iOS OpenCPN renders with OpenGL ES 2 through Qt (qopengl.h), like the
  Android build but without the Android GLES headers. Add an iOS branch next
  to the Android branch in the GL include blocks, use the GLES2 shader path
  and skip GL calls that GLES does not have.

Platform layer:
- Exclude code that needs IOKit, SocketCAN, CoreGraphics display IDs,
  serial ports or system(), none of which exist on iOS.
- Paths in the app sandbox: private data under Library/Application
  Support, shared data and translations in the app bundle, the log file
  in Documents so it shows in the Files app.
- Sound through AVFoundation; device GPS, compass and barometer through
  the existing Android internal-GPS driver, fed by the iOS app layer.
- Startup: create no windows before iOS reports the app active, show a
  busy indicator, no GL probe helper (OpenGL ES is always present), and
  plugin instrument panes float instead of docking.
- Safe-mode question as an alert; the online manual opens in Safari.
- svg_utils: hash long cache file names, which exceeded 255 characters in
  the iOS container.

Functions of the iOS app layer that the core calls are declared in the new
header model/include/model/ios_hooks.h; later commits add their own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
